#: ../../source/components_basic/29-component_ttmotor.rst:79
msgid "Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/29-component_ttmotor.rst:81
msgid "The first part of the code defines the motor control pins. These are connected to the L9110 motor control board."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/components_basic/29-component_ttmotor.rst:89
msgid "The ``setup()`` function initializes the motor control pins as output using the ``pinMode()`` function. Then it uses ``analogWrite()`` to set the speed of the motor. The value passed to ``analogWrite()`` can range from 0 (off) to 255 (full speed). A ``delay()`` function is then used to pause the code for 5000 milliseconds (or 5 seconds), after which the motor speed is set to 0 (off)."
msgstr ""

